<title>JAPAN: Aramco keeps July LPG prices unchanged - traders.</title>
<headline>Aramco keeps July LPG prices unchanged - traders.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's state-owned oil firm Saudi Aramco has set its July contract prices for propane at $175 per tonne, and butane at $192, both unchanged from June, traders said here on Monday.  </p>
<p>The propane price for July is up $15 from a year ago, while the price for butane is up $17 over the same period.</p>
<p>Saudi contract prices are loosely based on the results of three monthly spot tenders and the company's own assessment of spot market trends.</p>
</text>
